Privacy Policy for TileSum
Last updated: November 15, 2026

Zoran Ivanic (Kizo Games) ("we", "our", or "us") built the TileSum mobile game as a free application. This page is used to inform visitors and players regarding our policies with the collection, use, and disclosure of Personal Information if anyone decides to use our Service.

By downloading and playing TileSum, you agree to the collection and use of information in relation to this policy.

1. Information Collection and Use
We do not directly collect, store, or ask for personally identifiable information such as your name, physical address, phone number, or email address within the game. Game progress and local settings are stored locally on your device.

However, the application uses third-party services (such as game engines and advertising networks) that may automatically collect certain technical information used to identify your device, serve advertisements, and ensure app stability. This information may include:

Device Advertising ID (Google Advertising ID)

Device model, operating system version, and language settings

IP address (used for approximate location/region and ad delivery)

Crash logs, diagnostics, and basic gameplay interaction data

2. Third-Party Service Providers
TileSum relies on trusted third-party tools and SDKs to function and remain free to play. These third-party providers have their own Privacy Policies addressing how they use such data:

Google Play Services – https://www.google.com/policies/privacy/

Unity Technologies (Game Engine & Analytics) – https://unity.com/legal/privacy-policy

3. Advertising and Analytics
To keep TileSum free, we may display third-party advertisements (such as banner, interstitial, or rewarded video ads). Ad networks may use cookies, device identifiers, and similar technologies to serve personalized or non-personalized ads based on your region and consent settings. You can reset or opt out of personalized advertising at any time through your Android device settings (Settings > Google > Ads).

4. Data Retention and Security
We do not maintain external servers storing your personal profile. Any technical or diagnostic data collected by third-party SDKs (such as Unity or Google) is transmitted securely using standard encryption (HTTPS/TLS) and retained according to those providers' respective retention policies.

5. Children’s Privacy
TileSum is intended for a general audience and is not directed at children under the age of 13 (or the applicable age of digital consent in your country). We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children. If you are a parent or guardian and believe that your child has provided personal data through third-party services in our game, please contact us so we can take necessary action.

6. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Thus, you are advised to review this page periodically for any changes. Changes are effective immediately after they are posted on this page.

